actual material unit. Observation takes one round and 0.2 energy without sample consumption. Gather plus one physical trial therefore requires two action rounds, 2.5 energy and 0.1 unit of the gathered sample, excluding travel and normal world costs. Debit material exactly once; consumed trial material cannot also remain edible inventory. Retain the surviving quantity under existing ownership and decay rules; no food, reagent or replacement stock is created. Wet and heat modes must not fabricate their missing physical inputs; use only an executable supported mode. Report only the measured response implemented by that mode, with target/sample identity, mode, intensity, time, actual inputs, outcome and limitations. A mode name, visual appearance, softening, crushing, ordinary decay or lack of visible change cannot establish nutritional value, toxicity, absence of toxins or general edibility. No supported non-consumptive nutrition/toxicity assay is demonstrated in this registry: explicitly report those properties as unresolved without reading hidden resource values. Do not use eating, tasting or exposure of another participant as an implicit test. No health or satiety improvement results from inspection or sample testing. A complete probe is one indivisible interaction; interruption cancels it, with no resumable fractional test or completed evidence. Retry is a new action with newly validated inputs and costs. Preserve any already incurred effort or material loss; cancellation or death never regenerates spent inputs. Unconsumed material remains governed by existing inventory/death rules, with no duplicate refund. Gather uses its existing interruption and surviving-escrow rules. No persistent apparatus, ongoing trial, maintenance obligation or unattended treatment is created; remaining food continues ordinary ageing. Requests, learning and development/review waiting do not execute these actions or advance the world. Enforce these restrictions through the reused execution handler rather than repeated model adjudication.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":0,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Lin uses the existing zero-duration baseline individually; this review grants neither mastery nor evidence. No experience or wellbeing is earned for asking, reading the contract, naming a test, or receiving an unsupported-assay limitation. Only an actual event producing verified, personally applicable information, including genuinely informative physical failure, may enter existing evidence-deduplicated feedback. Repeated equivalent observations must not farm benefits; legitimate familiar practice may receive only whatever bounded benefit the established event rules already authorize. This reuse adds no reward formula, satisfaction source or protected-account mutation. Any existing benefit must retain its event-based cap, decay and cooldown; physical comfort remains capped at 10 and nutrition is never substituted by mood.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Render only actual observation or manipulation events using reusable metadata keyed by event ID, actor, target/sample ID, mode, intensity, progress/status and measured outcome. Reuse the visible plant or real sample appearance; do not create a laboratory, assay equipment, edible/safe marker, nutrition meter or success animation from the request. Distinguish completed observation or manipulation from a positive food-safety result: the former may succeed while nutrition and toxicity remain unresolved. Unsupported, interrupted and failed attempts must remain visibly unsupported, interrupted or failed and cannot show test success. Evidence visuals must refer to the actual execution event and measured property, not a generic capability-registration event.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

